<h2 style="text-align: center;">School Background</h2>
<p style="text-align: center;">Kyosiga Primary School is a private Chartered school owned
by the Registered Trustees of the Group One Association.
It was founded on 15th August 2004 when the associates
signed a Memorandum of Understanding with Uganda Martyrs
Primary to establish Kyosiga P/S.</p>
<em><strong>MORE INFORMATION</strong></em>

On 27th March 2009, the National Council for Education (NCE)
granted Kyosiga P/S a constituent primary status and it
became a nationally recognised primary school.

On 29th June 2015, NCE granted an independent operational
license to the Primary School under its new name,
Kyosiga P/S.

Kyosiga is a private Chartered school rooted in the Catholic
ethos but remains open to all those who qualify for its
programs. It is located 24 km from Kampala along the
Kampala-Entebbe Highway.

Blessed with a conducive learning and teaching environment,
Kyosiga is committed to remaining a hallmark and a niche
for quality education in Uganda and in the broader
East African region.
